# Valgrind suppressions for otterbrix Rust integration tests
# Format: https://valgrind.org/docs/manual/manual-core.html#manual-core.suppress
#
# Each entry must be accompanied by a comment explaining where the report
# came from and why it is being suppressed.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust std test runtime: TLS allocation for the per-thread mpmc context used
# by `test::run_tests` to collect CompletedTest events. The 48-byte block is
# pointed to from TLS that is torn down after Valgrind has already taken its
# leak snapshot, hence "possibly lost". This is a known artifact of Rust's
# `std::thread::current::init_current` path and has no relation to our code
# or to the libotterbrix C++ core.
{
   rust-std-test-runtime-mpmc-context-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:_ZN3std6thread6Thread3new*
   ...
}

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust std stack-overflow handler: per-thread metadata installed in a global
# BTreeMap by `std::sys::pal::unix::stack_overflow::thread_info::set_current_info`.
# Intentionally never freed (cannot run cleanup safely on signal-handler
# tear-down), so Valgrind reports it as "still reachable". Not our code.
{
   rust-std-stack-overflow-thread-info
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: reachable
   fun:malloc
   ...
   fun:_ZN3std3sys3pal4unix14stack_overflow11thread_info16set_current_info*
   ...
}
